($t$Xanthostemon verdugonianus$t$, $t$Xanthostemon verdugonianus$t$, $t$Myrtaceae$t$, $t$Famiglia botanica: Myrtaceae. Portamento: Tree. Altezza massima indicativa: 30 m. Xanthostemon verdugonianus or commonly known as Mangkono is a tree growing up to 50 m in height and 115 cm in bole diameter. It can be found in Southeast Asia particularly in the Philippines and is currently threatened by habitat loss. The bole is very irregular, fluted, and bent. Leaves are simple, relatively thick, alternate, and obovate. The inflorescence is red and located at terminal branches. The fruits are dehiscent with 2-3 lobes that split into 2-3 sections when ripe. The seeds are small and half-moon shaped. No plant part is of medicinal importance and edible. However, the plant is mainly valued for its excellent wood that is extremely hard, very heavy, and probably the most durable wood of the Philippines. It is of superior quality and is used for posts, piles, tool handles, wooden tool parts, bowling balls, dumbbells, paper weights, pulleys, rollers, etc.$t$, $j${"luce": "Pieno sole", "acqua": "Moderata", "terreno": "Tollera terreno: sabbioso/leggero, medio, argilloso/pesante"}$j$::jsonb, ARRAY[$t$Scheda in bozza, importata automaticamente da Plants For A Future (pfaf.org): dati non verificati manualmente, da controllare prima di considerarli affidabili$t$, $t$Nome comune (inglese, fonte PFAF): Mangkono$t$, $t$Rischi segnalati dalla fonte (testo originale in inglese, non tradotto per non alterarne il significato): None known$t$], $j${"irrigazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "concimazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "potatura": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "npk": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}}$j$::jsonb, $j${"famiglia_botanica": "Myrtaceae", "giorni_germinazione": null, "giorni_trapianto": null, "giorni_raccolta": null